    "title": "Daredevil: Born Again Returns for Season 2 - Here's When You Can Watch New Episodes",
    "text": "Plus your last chance to save on Disney+ and Hulu. After making his gaming debut in Clair Obscur: Expedition 33, Charlie Cox is once again donning the horned mask. Season 2 of Daredevil: Born Again premieres on Disney+ this week, continuing the MCU’s Phase 6 and bringing back the one and only Jessica Jones. Our Season 1 review highlighted a “strong core storyline and masterful lead performances” from Charlie Cox and Vincent d’Onofrio, and a particularly climactic season finale certainly set the stage for their continued rivalry in Season 2. If you’re hoping to tune in, here’s when you can expect new episodes of Daredevil: Born Again on Disney+. Daredevil: Born Again Season 2 Release Schedule Disney+ Daredevil: Born Again is streaming exclusively on Disney+. While Disney+ doesn’t offer its own free trial, you can technically try the service out for free through Hulu + Live TV. There are also plenty of bundle options. The second season of Daredevil: Born Again will premiere on March 24, 2026 and run for eight episodes total. New episodes will be released at 9pm ET/6pm PT every Tuesday, with a double episode dropping on March 31. After a series of time jumps in the revival’s first season, the new season picks up in the middle of the MCU’s Phase 6. We’ve gotten a couple of sneak peeks of what to expect from Season 2 in teasers and trailers, including a new Daredevil suit and the return of Jessica Jones. Daredevil: Born Again Season 2 - Official TrailerSince the first season, the Daredevil himself has also achieved a new world of fame from voicing Gustave in last year’s Game of the Year winner, Clair Obscur: Expedition 33. While Cox has continuously remarked that he isn’t a gamer, he recently revealed that he's already working on a new gaming project. What We Know About Season 3 Daredevil: Born Again has already been greenlit for a third season, with shooting starting this summer. As of now, Season 3 is scheduled to premiere in Spring 2027. We still have plenty of Phase 6 between now and then, including Spider-Man: Brand New Day and Avengers: Doomsday. You can check out the full MCU schedule for more details on that. Update (3/24): Disney has revealed that Episode 2 and 3 will debut on the same day. We've updated this story to reflect that.Blythe (she/her) is an Audience Development Coordinator at IGN who spends way too much time in character customization screens and tracking down collectibles. IGN LogoRecommendsIn This Article",
